---
// The Conway "game of life" background, settled off the bench at
// content/blog/theme-lab/components/GameOfLife.vue (docs/design.md, Settled,
// and docs/decisions-log.md). Plain canvas and a plain script, the same
// register as ThemeToggle/CodeTheme rather than a Vue island: this renders on
// every page through BaseLayout, and shipping Vue's runtime everywhere for a
// background field would be exactly the framework-on-every-page cost
// docs/design.md's Vue note argues against for post islands.
//
// No props: everything reader-adjustable lives in SettingsPanel.astro and its
// script talks to conway.ts directly (see the report), not through this
// component. `aria-hidden` because the canvas draws nothing a screen reader
// could use; the click-to-add-a-glider interaction is a bonus for a sighted
// pointer user, not a feature this needs to expose.
---

<canvas class="conway-field" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

<script>
  import '../scripts/conway'
</script>

<style>
  /*
   * z-index: -1 rather than a positive one on the content: header, main and
   * footer are ordinary in-flow boxes, so they already paint above a
   * negative-z-index fixed element without needing a z-index of their own.
   * That is also why a click on actual page text or a link still reaches
   * that element rather than the canvas underneath it, and why the field
   * only receives clicks in the room outside those boxes (the gutters, and
   * anywhere main's own exclusion mask has not already gone blank).
   */
  .conway-field {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    cursor: crosshair;
    touch-action: manipulation;
  }

  /* A reader who turned the field off in the settings panel gets this even
     if conway.ts fails to load at all: the attribute is set by the same
     blocking script that prevents a flash of the wrong theme. */
  :root[data-bg-life='off'] .conway-field {
    display: none;
  }
</style>
